<title>USA: Ultralife gets additional $1.26 mln orders.</title>
<headline>Ultralife gets additional $1.26 mln orders.</headline>
<dateline>NEWARK, N.J. 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ultralife Batteries Inc said on Monday that the United States Army, Communications and Electronics Command of Fort Monmouth, New Jersey exercised a contract option, valued at $1.26 million, to buy additional Ultralife lithium batteries.</p>
<p>Earlier this year, Ultralife began producing batteries under the initial contract which is now valued at more than $4 million.</p>
<p>The new contract option calls for production to continue throughout calendar 1997 and into calendar 1998.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
